# Context

## Background
Repository tidy-up after a full-tree review on 2026-11-08. The root
held 34 rules JSON files, 9 findings variants, and 3 one-off agent
prompt documents; the review judged most of that sprawl deliberate.

## Why This Way
- Only files with zero inbound references moved: a repo-wide sweep
  (excluding results/) found no importer or invocation of obs.py and
  no reference to the three prompt docs outside the group itself.
- rules_*.json and FINDINGS_*.md stayed put: findings cite exact
  paths, so moving them would break the evidence trail for no gain.
- Verified before commit: 210 Python unittests pass, all four Node
  suites pass (web_ui SKIP without jsdom, as documented), and the
  web board regenerates byte-identical.

## Gotchas
- The A4 print kit regenerates content-identical but not
  byte-identical: ReportLab embeds CreationDate/ModDate and derives
  the document /ID from them. Pinning an invariant date in
  make_a4_print_kit.py would make regeneration byte-stable.
- obs.py resolves sim.py relative to the working directory, so run
  it from the repo root (true before the move as well).
